        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<div class=\"description\">\nFolio 25v of the Lindisfarne Gospels, showing St Matthew, writing. He is accompanied by his symbol, a winged man blowing a trumpet and carrying a book (captioned <i>imago hominis</i>). A figure holding a book peers out from behind a curtain; for a possible explanation of this, see <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://durham-repository.worktribe.com/output/1634142/lindisfarne-and-the-gospels-the-art-of-interpretation\"><i>Lindisfarne and the Gospels: The Art of Interpretation</i>,</a> pp. 9–11. The main caption reads <i><a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E1%BD%81\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikt:ὁ\">Ὁ</a> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E1%BC%85%CE%B3%CE%B9%CE%BF%CF%82\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikt:ἅγιος\">AGIOS</a> MATTHEUS</i> (\"the saint Matthew\").</div>",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
        "DateTimeOriginal": {
          "value": "between 710 and 721",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
